      "message": "When I look on how `L2CA_EnableUpdateBleConnParams` and how `l2cble_start_conn_update(p_lcb);` works please confirm my understanding\n\nThis function has following work to do\n\n1. Check if there is \"lock\" already set by service discovery - if so return.\n2. Check if there is \"lock\" set by audio profile - if so return.\n3. there was no LOCK and If `lock` is true then underlying function `l2cble_start_conn_update(p_lcb)` will start connection parameter request using parameters stored in \"p_lcb\". Is it anyhow important what parameters are there? Are we somehow confident what parameters are there or it does not matter?\n\n4. If  `lock` is false - then underlying `l2cble_start_conn_update(p_lcb)` will go back to default connection parameters .\n\nIs my understanding correct?  \n\nIf so I suggest the new API should look like this.\n\ntypedef enum {\nL2CA_CONN_PARAM_USER_STACK_SERV_DISCOVERY,\nL2CA_CONN_PARAM_USER_AUDIO_STACK,\n} l2ca_conn_param_user_t;\n\n\nL2CA_RequestToProceedConnParamUpdate(l2ca_conn_param_user_t user, RawAddress\u0026 address);\nL2CA_RequestDefaultConnParam(l2ca_conn_param_user_t user, RawAddress\u0026 address);",
